{"title":"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Compute the number of ways to fill in the following magic square such that:\n</p><p>1. the product of all rows, columns, and diagonals are equal (the sum condition is waived),\n</p><p>2. all entries are <i>nonnegative</i> integers less than or equal to ten, and\n</p><p>3. entries CAN repeat in a column, row, or diagonal.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/f/15fdbd63c43e4345cf06b18956239b7aa40ec839.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(100); defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)); int i; for(i=0; i&lt;4; i=i+1) { draw((0,2*i)--(6,2*i)^^(2*i,0)--(2*i,6)); } label(&quot;$1$&quot;, (1,5)); label(&quot;$9$&quot;, (3,5)); label(&quot;$3$&quot;, (1,1)); [/asy]\" width=\"168\" height=\"168\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the \"common product\" of the magic square (i.e. the product of each row, diagonal, and column). There are now two cases: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/f/cdff03e9720b5bcdcc4d05924a552425889f3960.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/5/b456ed4aac07cca7fe4c23bd7fd4f75d90f6b6e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/a/64ace8b7b9281a9e549e38af277a0e3f2d47a516.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline{\\text{Case 1: } P \\neq 0.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"114\" height=\"21\" /> Let the top right corner be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, as in the picture below. Then, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/9/50938e03cc658419c401385c6937d23d79814ec4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=9n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, so the middle left cell must have a value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/5/a45e3d817886b4d9dbd6bb74ad23463ed139ed68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/1/cf1f7d5a0b26a9118943f7a9916acc3b858ca1a4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(100); defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)); int i; for(i=0; i&lt;4; i=i+1) { draw((0,2*i)--(6,2*i)^^(2*i,0)--(2*i,6)); } label(&quot;$1$&quot;, (1,5)); label(&quot;$9$&quot;, (3,5)); label(&quot;$3$&quot;, (1,1)); label(&quot;$n$&quot;, (5,5)); label(&quot;$3n$&quot;, (1,3)); [/asy]\" width=\"168\" height=\"168\" />\n</p><p>Looking at the diagonal which stretches from the bottom left to the top right, we see that the central cell must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Then, by looking at the other diagonal, we see that the bottom right cell must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/5/a45e3d817886b4d9dbd6bb74ad23463ed139ed68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/0/56062d1a0b7fc55c9c6d8744bf052e122881a3c1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(100); defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)); int i; for(i=0; i&lt;4; i=i+1) { draw((0,2*i)--(6,2*i)^^(2*i,0)--(2*i,6)); } label(&quot;$1$&quot;, (1,5)); label(&quot;$9$&quot;, (3,5)); label(&quot;$3$&quot;, (1,1)); label(&quot;$n$&quot;, (5,5)); label(&quot;$3n$&quot;, (1,3)); label(&quot;$3$&quot;, (3,3)); label(&quot;$3n$&quot;, (5,1)); [/asy]\" width=\"168\" height=\"168\" />\n</p><p>Looking at the bottom row, we see that the bottom central cell has a value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and looking at the middle row tells us that the right middle cell also has a value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/b/8eba51872e4b7ace044c303b4c9422228db3c868.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(100); defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)); int i; for(i=0; i&lt;4; i=i+1) { draw((0,2*i)--(6,2*i)^^(2*i,0)--(2*i,6)); } label(&quot;$1$&quot;, (1,5)); label(&quot;$9$&quot;, (3,5)); label(&quot;$3$&quot;, (1,1)); label(&quot;$n$&quot;, (5,5)); label(&quot;$3n$&quot;, (1,3)); label(&quot;$3$&quot;, (3,3)); label(&quot;$3n$&quot;, (5,1)); label(&quot;$1$&quot;, (3,1)); label(&quot;$1$&quot;, (5,3)); [/asy]\" width=\"168\" height=\"168\" />\n</p><p>Looking at the central column, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/f/8bf17971894b3f681b3dc8b6084b24a403cce052.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 1 = P = 9n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"138\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5635737307f5f0651cced8ee2e6558a426fd27b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/078676613157d561f54ea65bc221b495c32e1416.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n=9 \\leq 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" /> and all the rows, diagonals, and columns multiply to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1051e7d41ec0b8bd688a872be17538413f4ee97b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5635737307f5f0651cced8ee2e6558a426fd27b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> satisfies the constriants of the problem. Thus, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/f/cdff03e9720b5bcdcc4d05924a552425889f3960.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" />, we have only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possibility for the magic square.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/ccc525a34707c09abb0c4cdbdfe2674f99935e82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline{\\text{Case 2: }P=0.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" /> Because only one cell remains on both the left column and the top row, their remaining cells must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, as shown below:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/1/15161157fb2f2d94c538eff852eda8a046eea26d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(100); defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)); int i; for(i=0; i&lt;4; i=i+1) { draw((0,2*i)--(6,2*i)^^(2*i,0)--(2*i,6)); } label(&quot;$1$&quot;, (1,5)); label(&quot;$9$&quot;, (3,5)); label(&quot;$3$&quot;, (1,1)); label(&quot;$0$&quot;, (5,5)); label(&quot;$0$&quot;, (1,3)); [/asy]\" width=\"168\" height=\"168\" />\n</p><p>Now, we still need to place zeroes in the top left to bottom right diagonal, the middle column, and the bottom row. Placing a zero in the right middle cell will bring us no closer to this goal, so it can be any integer inclusively between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and thus it can take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> possible states. Let the three remaining cells be called \"special cells.\" Placing two zeroes in any of the special cells will ensure that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/5/b456ed4aac07cca7fe4c23bd7fd4f75d90f6b6e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />, so we have another free cell which can also take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> different values.\n</p><p>To prevent overcounting, we now have two cases. In the first case, <b>only</b> two of the special cells are zero, and so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/6/4c65582d5a3f4ed3a2d3ea55c7a466d4a1de6f85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\choose 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"22\" height=\"27\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/1/371fc9459410350e9cfee5f0e6eb3d0c68a7b48f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cdot 10 \\cdot 11 = 330$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities, because the third special cell cannot be zero. In the second case, all three special cells are zero, so we have only the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> possibilities for the middle right cell. Adding these two numbers together, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/6/f56f95192f2b1e4618cb7e4a27b12a0244eae404.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$330+11=341$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Remembering to add the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> possibility from Case 1, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/2/7e2354af48ba162c85571041a39f21a9d0a7f43f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$341+1=\\boxed{342}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"123\" height=\"25\" /> as our final answer.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems\">2013 Mock AIME I Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">Preceded by Problem 3</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">Followed by Problem 5</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017232816\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.031 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 188/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7726/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:28342:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017232816 and revision id 223960. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}